'' The runtime inventory. docs/plan/11 section 3: no 'fb_StrAssign' string literal
'' anywhere else in tiko-lang, so that there is ONE place to audit against the runtime and
'' a dumpable list that can be diffed against the library's real exports.
''
'' The full differential -- return type, arity and every parameter type, plus a
'' cross-check that each name is an exported symbol of libfb.a -- is
'' tools/gen/check-rtl.sh, which needs fbc present. This is the part that does not.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-rtl tests/rtl/src/empty.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrAssign ptr (ptr, i64, ptr, i64, i32)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrDelete void (ptr)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrCompare i32 (ptr, i64, ptr, i64)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ArrayRedimEx i32 (ptr, i64, i32, i32, i64, ...)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ThreadCreate ptr (ptr, ptr, i64)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrAssignMid void (ptr, i64, i64, ptr)
'' fb_UStrToStr is the 520th: 'val( <ustring> )' converts through it (tests/mir/val-ustring).
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrToStr ptr (ptr, i64)
'' AND FOUR MORE FOR THE NON-LOCAL ERROR JUMP, 2026-09-20. 'ON ERROR GOTO' installs a
'' handler in one procedure and the throw may be in another; LLVM cannot branch across
'' functions, so the compiler setjmps where the handler is installed and the runtime
'' longjmps into it. Two of the four are the C library's own setjmp under the two names
'' it has: tiko links ucrtbase, which exports '__intrinsic_setjmp' and not '_setjmp'.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ErrorJmpBuf ptr ()
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ErrorGetHandler ptr ()
'' AND TWO MORE FOR THE USTRING OUTPUT ENTRY POINTS, 2026-09-22: WRITE and PRINT USING
'' had none, and sent a ustring through the narrow pair as UTF-16 bytes.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WriteUStr void (i32, ptr, i32)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintUsingUStr i32 (i32, ptr, i32)
'' AND TWO MORE FOR INSTR'S 'any' FORMS OVER A USTRING, 2026-09-23: tiko-rt defines both
'' and the lowering declined, believing there were none.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrInstrAny i64 (i64, ptr, i64, ptr, i64)
'' AND THREE MORE, 2026-09-26: fb_UStrTrimEx and its L and R twins, the pattern form of
'' trim over a ustring (tests/mir/ustring-trim-pattern).
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrRTrimEx ptr (ptr, i64, ptr, i64)
'' TWO MORE, 2026-10-02: fb_InputUStr and fb_FileLineInputUStr, a ustring's readers (T66).
'' ONE MORE, 2026-10-06: fb_UStrSwap, SWAP of two ustrings (tests/codegen/swap-ustring).
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrSwap void (ptr, i64, ptr, i64)
'' TWO MORE, 2026-10-17: fb_WstrAssignToAUtf8 and fb_hPathRename, the classic file statements'
'' Unicode paths (tests/codegen/unicode-paths-run).
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_hPathRename i32 (ptr, ptr)
'' FIVE MORE, 2026-11-06: tkort_IfaceFind, tkort_ObjIfaceFind, tkort_IfaceTryCast,
'' tkort_ObjIfaceTryCast and tkort_IfaceTypeCast, interfaces' run-time search (lib/rt/src/oop/
'' iface.tiko, tests/codegen/iface-dynamic-run).
'' EXPECT-OUT: tkort_IfaceFind ptr (ptr, ptr, ptr)
'' SIX MORE, 2026-11-19: int128 / uint128's STR, PRINT and WRITE, tiko's own and so 'tko_' --
'' the value as two i64s, low half first (lib/rt/src/str/tostr.tiko, tests/codegen/int128-run).
'' EXPECT-OUT: tko_Int128ToStr ptr (i64, i64)
'' EXPECT-OUT: tko_PrintInt128 void (i32, i64, i64, i32)
'' EXPECT-OUT: tko_WriteUInt128 void (i32, i64, i64, i32)
'' TWELVE MORE, 2026-11-19: int128's WSTR pair, HEX/OCT/BIN and the wide forms, INPUT, READ
'' and the PRINT USING pair (tests/codegen/int128-p2-run). INPUT and READ take the address.
'' EXPECT-OUT: tko_HEX128 ptr (i64, i64, i32)
'' EXPECT-OUT: tko_InputInt128 i32 (ptr)
'' EXPECT-OUT: tko_PrintUsingInt128 i32 (i32, i64, i64, i32)
'' EXPECT-OUT: rtl: 561 entries
